From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:10:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] feat(selection): transcript reaction words and facecam
 mouth check for streamer reactions

Adds a "lexical" voice-family signal from transcript words (exclamations,
'!' marks, quick repeats; en/es/romanised Hindi). build_reaction_hints loads
the cached transcript words itself, so video_service.py is unchanged. Words
alone never create a moment (the two-signal rule still applies).

Adds a mouth-movement check (YuNet landmarks in the facecam): a voice-led
reaction whose facecam mouth stays still and face is calm is demoted as
likely game dialogue. Fails open when the face is not visible.

Real-sample proxy (Twitch, weak transcript labels, see EVIDENCE.md):
3 extra picks; the mouth check demoted nothing in these samples.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
